Source: review/opencode/packages/core/src/plugin/provider/opencode.ts:332,344
(OPENCODE_API_KEY read as credentials); :180-260 (model catalog fetched from
the Console with that credential — which is why the 2.0.26 CLI, with no local
opencode-go catalog, lists nothing standalone while serve resolves the id).

## Observation
- Serve DOES pick up OPENCODE_API_KEY from the environment: with the key,
  the provider attempts authentication upstream (Go-plan quota refusal for
  the exact AGENCY_MODEL id), and the entrypoint refuses to start without
  it (exit 64, checks 03). No `auth import` step is needed.
- `opencode models` in the 2.0.26 container does NOT list AGENCY_MODEL:
  --standalone prints nothing (rc=0); the default form fails EROFS on the
  read-only config dir. The host 2.0.28 CLI lists it (5 muse-spark lines).
  Server-side resolution is proven by the quota error above, so the CLI
  listing is a display quirk, and the fleet (Stage 1c) uses HTTP, never it.
- The model id needs no correction: the server accepted it verbatim.

## Verdict: partly (env pickup yes; container CLI listing no, host CLI yes,
server-side resolution yes; no fallback adopted)
